      '**Body surface area (BSA)** is used for chemotherapy and some pediatric drugs. The Mosteller formula: BSA (m²) = √(height in cm × weight in kg ÷ 3,600). Older rules estimated children’s doses from adult doses: **Clark’s rule** (child’s weight in lb ÷ 150 × adult dose) and **Young’s rule** (age ÷ (age + 12) × adult dose). They appear on some tests but are not used for modern prescribing.',
